  "artifact": "Feature: Alarms\n\n  Scenario: Medium severity alarm\n    Given the system is initialized\n    When a medium severity alarm is triggered\n    Then the alarm should be indicated with a yellow color\n    And the alarm should have a flashing frequency of 0.5Hz with a 50% duty cycle\n\n  Scenario: High severity alarm with 10 pulses\n    Given the system is initialized\n    When a high severity alarm is triggered\n    Then the alarm should have an auditory signal consisting of 10 pulses with each pulse lasting 200ms\n    And the pulse frequency should be 500Hz\n\n  Scenario: High severity alarm with 4 pulses\n    Given the system is initialized\n    When a high severity alarm is triggered\n    Then the alarm should have an auditory signal consisting of 4 pulses with each pulse lasting 200ms\n    And the pulse frequency should be 500Hz\n\n  Scenario: Audio pause key press\n    Given the system is initialized and alarms are active\n    When the AUDIO PAUSE / ALARM PAUSE key is pressed\n    Then all active alarms should be paused for 60 seconds\n    And the alarm activation symbol should be displayed with the symbol IEC 60417-5576\n\n  Scenario: Apnea alarm\n    Given the system is initialized and apnea time interval is exceeded\n    When no breath is triggered\n    Then a medium priority alarm should be triggered with the display text \"APNEA ALARM\"\n\n  Scenario: High breath rate alarm\n    Given the system is initialized and breath rate exceeds the setting\n    When the breath rate is exceeded\n    Then a medium level alarm should be triggered with the display text \"HIGH BREATH RATE\"\n\n  Scenario: Low pressure alarm\n    Given the system is initialized and pressure is low\n    When a low pressure alarm is triggered\n    Then a high severity alarm should be triggered with the display text \"LOW INSP P\"\n\n  Scenario Outline: Maximum breath rate setting\n    Given the system is initialized\n    When the breath rate is set to <breath_rate>\n    Then the maximum breath rate setting should be <max_breath_rate>\n    And the alarm threshold should be <max_breath_rate>\n\n    Examples:\n      | breath_rate | max_breath_rate |\n      |-------------|-----------------|\n      | 12          | 12              |\n      | 15          | 15              |\n      | 20          | 20              |\n      | 25          | 25              |\n      | 30          | 30              |",
